Description: scene: Keep the padding of a scaled surface's damage inside the surface
 .
 The damage of a surface that is not drawn at its buffer's size (a film larger
 than the output, a viewport, a fractional scale) was grown by a pixel on every
 side to cover the filtering between pixels, and the grown region was not cut at
 the surface. A full screen window therefore damaged the output next to it, which
 rendered a frame for each picture of the film though nothing on it changed (the
 A10's 3D film on a laptop panel with a frame packing TV, 20 frames a second,
 after the side by side width fix only handled a buffer drawn at its own size).
 .
 The padding stays inside the surface's rectangle. testStereoOutputRepaint gains
 the A10's cases (the film larger or smaller than the output through a viewport,
 the other output on the left, the film's output in a 3D mode too, a 2D film):
 5 of them failed with 25 of 25 pictures before the change.
